```alloy
@cfg(server)
function save(player: Player) end

@cfg(client and not studio)
const hud = build_hud()
```
Code for one side. A function keeps its type and opens with the check: called where the condition fails, it raises. A local reads its value only where the condition holds, and stays typed as the value; elsewhere it is nil.

The conditions: `server`, `client`, `studio`, `edit`, `running`, and `test` (an `alloy test` run). Join them with `not`, `and`, `or`, or `any(...)` and `all(...)`. A shared module loads on both sides, so the runtime reads RunService when the code runs.

**Applies to** `function` · `local`

